    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0340" n="260" xml:id="pg260"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fesler to Mr.
                            Hill</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Amoy, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * I beg to inform the Department that
                    on July 23, under instructions from the minister, I entered a strong protest
                    under Article XIV of the French treaty with China and the favored-nation clause
                    in our treaty, copy of which is herewith inclosed, as well as a copy of the
                    taotai’s reply. I am reporting to the legation for further instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John H. Fesler</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed></closer>




